  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Options for the retry budget that limits the number of retries relative to the number of requests.
            </summary>
    <remarks>
            The retry budget tracks the number of requests and retries over a sliding window of <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions.SamplingDuration" />.
            Once the window contains at least <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions.MinimumThroughput" /> requests, a retry is only allowed while the number
            of retries in the window is below <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions.RetryRatio" /> multiplied by the number of requests, rounded down.
            At least one retry per window is always allowed, unless <see cref="P:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.HttpRetryBudgetOptions.RetryRatio" /> is 0, which suppresses every retry.
            When the budget is exhausted, the outcome that would have been retried is returned to the caller instead and the
            <c>OnRetryBudgetExhausted</c> resilience event is reported with <see cref="T:Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience.OnRetryBudgetExhaustedArguments" />.
            <para>
            The budget prevents retry storms: when a dependency is degraded, retries can multiply the load on it by up to
            <c>MaxRetryAttempts + 1</c>. A budget caps that amplification to roughly <c>1 + RetryRatio</c>.
            </para><para>
            A budget instance is shared by all requests that use the same resilience pipeline instance. Each named client
            (and each authority when <c>SelectPipelineByAuthority</c> is used) has its own budget.
            The budget is reset when the pipeline is reloaded due to options changes.
            </para></remarks>
  </Docs>
